Adversarial review of the archon-cli `feat/evidence-curation` change set (~32 commits since `926285ad`) COMPLETE 2026-07-13. Ran archon's OWN reviewer agent personas (security-logic-auditor, control-flow-analyzer, concurrency-analyzer, business-logic-auditor) one-per-subsystem via a working runtime, each CONFIRM/REFUTE-ing the plan's hypotheses against real source. Results: `~/projects/archon-cli/plans/adversarial-review-RESULTS-2026-07-13.md`; plan `plans/adversarial-review-plan-2026-07-13.md`. Nothing committed/changed — review only.

**All 5 plan hotlist hypotheses CONFIRMED + 1 extra CRITICAL. Six criticals:**
- CR-1 `docs delete "" / . -y` prefix-resolves to the WHOLE corpus, no gate (`docs_reprocess.rs:139-177`).
- CR-2 `docs reprocess` shares that resolver, NO confirmation at all + destructive-first (clears evidence before pipeline).
- CR-3 `verify_bank` locates text corpus-wide, never binds to the CITED source (`verify.rs:110`); tie-break picks LOWER page → primary quote verifies against a secondary work while draft renders the primary cite — defeats the verbatim guarantee. Same in `link_cited_sources`.
- CR-4 seeded 2-up remap applied UNCONDITIONALLY (`ingest_pdf.rs:163`); a 1-up doc w/ a seed doubles page stride.
- CR-5 stale HNSW snapshot: `manifest.vector_count` never read → docs ingested after `vector-compact` are INVISIBLE to semantic search (`vector_store.rs:236`).
- CR-6 sticky `model_failed` has no reset path, bricks the text embedder for the process life (`embed_fastembed.rs:26`).

Top fix priority: the 2 data-loss footguns (CR-1/CR-2), then the verbatim gate (CR-3). Plus 9 High (2-up gutter/side, inline-Bekker false positive, uncapped exact-path p.0, hash-chain doesn't recompute bbox/page from live rows, non-atomic teardown, trim/cite seam, NearVerbatim≥0.9 gate). Our enrichment deadlock fix + trim substring invariant + owning_work_docs author-anchoring all held up (REFUTED cleanly).

**COMMITTED 2026-07-14 as `2bf98d8a` on `feat/evidence-curation` (WSL/PROTEUS, local only — NOT pushed; branch is 2 ahead of `fcdp/feat/evidence-curation` incl. the earlier local `c0f7e3ce` o-viewer). Single commit, 38 files +4835/-511 — the five logical groups share files (curate/draft/pack/data_actions/lib.rs) + no hunk-staging available, so grouped by commit-message sections. Push awaits user permission.** Everything below is now IN that commit.

**FIXES IMPLEMENTED 2026-07-14 (committed 2bf98d8a).** All 6 criticals + 9 high + 7 med + 5 low fixed on `feat/evidence-curation` via a 6-owner workflow (disjoint files); 26 files, +3028/-393. Build GREEN (0 err/0 warn), ALL affected-crate tests pass (~2140, 0 failed) incl. new tests (delete-resolver exact-only, tamper legacy-v1 backward-compat, CR-3 wrong-source). Backups: `.backups/adversarial-fixes-20260713-204503/` (+ _HEAD.txt). NOT committed (per verify-before-commit rule) — commit from WSL only after user sign-off. Residuals flagged: CR-2 runs the pipeline TWICE (probe+real, reprocess cost 2x; true stage-and-swap deferred); B6 image/figure recto-vs-verso side stays verso+warning (per-figure side detection deferred, needs gutter data); H-5 bbox tamper-detection is v2-only (new ingests) — existing corpus verifies under v1 (content/page tamper detected, bbox not) until reingest, by design non-breaking. A mid-run API outage killed the workflow's auto build/test; completed manually (1 seam fix: docs.rs dispatch for new enum fields).

**ALSO uncommitted on `feat/evidence-curation` (same branch, 2026-07-14): three drafting knobs SHIPPED** (build+tests green 1210/0): `--target-words N|LO-HI` + `--draft-type section|subsection|chapter|article|note` on `archon draft` (overrides) & `evidence curate`; `--collection`/`--source` scope on `evidence curate` + `--source` on `evidence find` (new `DiscoverOptions.sources`); `DraftType` enum in archon-draft (genre note additive to FCDP prompt, `Section`⇒byte-identical). PLUS **seamless curate→draft handoff SHIPPED** 2026-07-14: `archon evidence curate --out <dir>` persists a draftable pack (knobs baked in, gp_validate-gated, reuses `/curate` write path) + `--draft [--workdir W]` chains into the FCDP run (one-command curate→draft); knobs live in the pack so ALL draft paths honour them (the `/draft`-wizard-doesn't-forward-flags gap is now moot). Backups `.backups/three-knobs-20260714-054732/` + `.backups/curate-out-20260714-063812/`. PLUS **guided-draft CLI wizard SHIPPED** 2026-07-14: `archon draft` with NO pack (in a TTY) launches a step-by-step stdin flow folding curation in — question → scope → RA proposes → keep/drop review → draft-type → word-count → write pack → run FCDP → review-outcome; non-TTY bails with a hint; `archon draft <pack>` + flags stay the fast path. `Commands::Draft` pack/workdir now Option; `run_draft_wizard` + `parse_drop_list` (tested) in draft.rs. Backup `.backups/draft-wizard-20260714-070635/`. PLUS two bug-fixes 2026-07-14 from live wizard testing: (a) **RA tool-turn ceiling 16→40 + recover a submitted selection** instead of hard-failing (`curate_agent.rs` — `run_agentic_tool_loop` returns `LlmError::Unsupported` "exceeded N tool turns"; `build_result` reads the submitted selection from state so it's recoverable); (b) **embedded default gate config** (`archon-draft` `DEFAULT_GATE_CONFIG_JSON`/`default_gate_config()` via include_str! of `crates/archon-draft/data/ga-gate-locked-v2.json`) + fallback in `handle_draft_command` AND the `/draft` preflight — a curated pack references the gate by bare name but it was never written next to the pack, so ANY curated pack failed to draft (`read gate config … No such file`); explicit `--gate-config` missing still errors. So this branch now carries FOUR feature change-sets (review fixes + knobs + seamless handoff + guided wizard) + these two wizard bug-fixes, all build+tests green — a commit decision must account for all; suggest separate logical commits from WSL after sign-off. Backups `.backups/ra-turn-cap-20260714-074059/` + `.backups/gate-embed-20260714-075613/`. PLUS two curation-quality fixes from the first live draft (Aristotle phantasia): (c) **strip leading OCR running-head/locator line** from quotes in `trim_to_relevant_span` (`quote_trim.rs` — a Bekker header "II, 414b13-416a9\n\n" leaked into the sealed quote + draft; strip returns a SUFFIX so it stays exact-substring/verbatim; tested); (d) **dedup identical quotes** in `curation_to_pack` (curate.rs — RA can seal the same passage twice → repeated in draft; dedup on (source,text) BEFORE assemble_pack numbers Qn so reanchor_cites stays 1:1). Also hand-patched the one existing test pack (`curated-packs/define-aristotle-…/`) — dropped the dup + stripped the header → 2 quotes, verify-bank exact-1.00 both, draft-ready (backup `.backups/existing-pack-patch-20260714-084305/`). Live wizard→draft run WORKS end-to-end (STOP-AND-SURFACE on soft style gates is normal). PLUS (e) **FCDP thinking-off recovery** (`fable.rs` `call`): the Opus adaptive-thinking-ate-the-whole-budget flake (empty output at the 32k ceiling, stop_reason None/max_tokens) used to ABORT the whole draft run; now on that empty it retries the stage ONCE with thinking+effort disabled (`call_once` gained a `thinking: bool`) so the model emits the answer — only a still-empty retry aborts. Known-latent from the draft: FCDP soft-gate misses (opacity band, G3 evidentiary-weight judge) are per-run, human-reviewed via `evidence review-outcome`. Details: [[project-archon-evidence-curation-plan]] TODO `plans/curation-drafting-system-todo-2026-07-11.md`.

**Non-obvious infra fact:** `archon pipeline run <spec>` (the declarative multi-agent pipeline) is NON-FUNCTIONAL — `pipeline_declarative.rs:23` uses `DefaultTaskService::new` (queue=None) and no production `AgentExecutor`/`TaskExecutor` is ever wired, so every step sits Pending and the run hangs ~30min to the step timeout (looks like a deadlock: all tokio workers futex-parked at 0% CPU). NOT the embedding/Cozo path (that's `pipeline code`/`research`). `archon chat` works. So to "run through archon" today, the pipeline path needs executor wiring first. Related: [[project-archon-evidence-curation-plan]], [[project-icp-drafting-analysis-report]].
