**DRAFTING-SYSTEM FUTURE-WORK TODO + WS2 CRASH/BLOAT FIX (2026-07-11).** Organized implementation plan for 7 user future-work items + the *Drafting System Update Proposal* + live-run findings: `~/projects/archon-cli/plans/curation-drafting-system-todo-2026-07-11.md` (WS0 quick-wins/foldering/★-bug · WS1 source-scope+two-step primary/secondary+local-toggle · WS2 draft-quality · WS3 staged proposal→draft pipeline mapped onto FCDP · WS4 TUI clarity · WS5 gauntlet deep-dive; status markers ✅/✏️/⏸/❌/🆕; critiques: DON'T expose raw FCDP prompt=breaks provenance, gauntlet checks already exist, online deferred, per-source index is a prereq). **✅ WS2 quote-granularity crash+bloat fix DONE — committed `ac7bd3b4` on `feat/evidence-curation` (WSL, NOT pushed; the WS2 rollback point). Build re-verified green + archon-evidence 35/0 (2026-07-11). RESUME = WS★ implementation.** **WS★ FEASIBILITY VERDICT (2026-07-11, read-only 4-probe workflow): BACKFILL-migration CONFIRMED FEASIBLE — NO GPU/Marker reingest needed.** Persisted+usable: `doc_chunks{page_start,page_end,content,content_hash}` (single-page chunks → exact, offset0=page_start, covers the majority) + `doc_chunk_spatial{page_num,blocks(JSON page-grouped),coord_space}` (marker per-page block counts) + `doc_sources.source_path` (PDFs still on disk → CPU re-derive). ONLY missing datum = intra-chunk char offset of each page boundary (`PageOffset[]` dropped after chunking) — recoverable CPU-only: `coord_space=='none'` chunks byte-exact via pdftotext -layout + `compute_pdf_page_offsets` + deterministic re-chunk + `content_hash` align; `coord_space=='marker'` via anchor last/first page-line into stored content, fallback per-page block counts. **PLAN:** add relation `doc_chunk_page_breaks{chunk_id, char_offset_in_chunk => page}` (BYTE space); backfill per-doc (idempotent); wire `store::get_chunk_page_breaks` into `quote_verify.rs build_location` (~L227-236) — replace coarse `page_start.min()/page_end.max()` with per-hit `local=(a-orig_start)` → `page_for(local)`, THREADING the matched span `(a,b)` (find_fragment_bboxes L162-166) + each hit chunk's `orig_start` (`doc.chunk_ranges`) into build_location. **KEY RISK: query-time `(a,b)` is in doc-RECONSTRUCTED-CONCATENATION byte space (chunks joined by injected `\n`), NOT chunk-local — must translate `local=a-orig_start` via `Reconstructed.chunk_ranges`; PageOffset uses BYTE offsets despite `char_*` naming.** SCOPE=PAGE-accuracy ONLY: sentence-tight BBOX narrowing is OUT (doc_chunk_spatial.blocks = pure geometry, NO text→box offset map → would itself need reingest-quality data). Fuzzy match path (quote_verify L192-204) emits no `(a,b)` → sub-span page-res applies to EXACT path only unless extended. Marker multi-page chunks = the weak point (heuristic, not byte-exact but reliably picks the correct PAGE since boundaries are 100s–1000s of chars apart). Reserve reingest ONLY if audit shows interleaved-reading-order Marker chunks defeating the anchor. Confidence medium. **DECISION 2026-07-11: P2 (ingestion-schema upgrade + REINGEST) CHOSEN over backfill (P1)** — user is OK to reingest (fast on their GPU), and P2 is the ONLY path to sentence-tight bbox + the Q3 full-page-red-box `o` viewer + Bekker loci; it also makes page-breaks byte-exact on ALL chunks (not heuristic on Marker chunks). **TEST-FIRST (user directive):** code changes → reingest+validate ONE hard doc FIRST = O'Gorman (`corpus/rhetorical_ontology/O'Gorman, Ned - Aristotle's Phantasia…(2005)_[My Copy].pdf` — 13 LANDSCAPE **2-up** sheets @792×612pts = worst-case layout) → only THEN reingest the rest of the 126-PDF corpus. **Bekker/locator fix BUNDLED into the same reingest**, gated on filename prefix `Aristotle - ` (user: in this corpus ONLY Aristotle texts carry Bekker); test Bekker on `corpus/rhetorical_ontology/Aristotle - On Memory_(2014)_[Clean Copy].pdf` (9pp single-page). O'Gorman is SECONDARY (filename `O'Gorman…`) → must get NO Bekker, isolating the layout test from the Bekker test. Concrete P2 build plan under investigation (6-probe workflow) → saved to `plans/p2-ingestion-upgrade-build-plan-2026-07-11.md` (6-probe-derived, code-anchored file:line throughout) — AWAITING SIGN-OFF before any ingestion code. **CORPUS SCAN 2026-07-11: 10/126 PDFs are LANDSCAPE/2-up** (O'Gorman NOT unique — also Heidegger FCM, 3 Caston Aristotle papers, Nussbaum De Motu, 2 Heim) → the sheet→logical-page formula MUST be DATA-DRIVEN (running-head-derived), not an O'Gorman hard-seed. **Top catches from the plan:** `page_num`=physical PDF SHEET (`marker.rs:105-124`) so 2-up cites are currently WRONG/ambiguous (O'Gorman sheet1 = book pp.16|17; 13 sheets→26 pp, book 16–41); `DocVectorStore` has NO delete method → add `delete_vectors_for_doc` BEFORE any reingest or a re-chunk orphans vectors → stale HNSW hits corpus-wide; Bekker glyph = literal `*` inline (`450*1`) glued to line-ends, current `bekker_re` misses it (needs inline scan + char class `[abAB*ªº]`); the two new relations must fold into `spatial_hash`/`commit_hash` (`chunk.rs:132`); O'Gorman is NOT yet ingested (fresh `docs ingest`, not reprocess). New schema: `doc_chunk_blocks{chunk_id,block_idx=>char_start,char_end,page,x0..y1}` + `doc_chunk_page_breaks{chunk_id,offset_in_chunk=>page}` (BYTE offsets). Query wiring = `quote_verify.rs build_location` per-break lookup, translating the match `(a,b)` from doc-CONCATENATION space (C) → chunk-local (B) via `Reconstructed.chunk_ranges` (byte-exact ONLY on exact path; fuzzy falls back to range). `o` viewer (P5) ships WITHOUT reingest (full page + red super_box), swaps to sentence-tight box post-reingest. Open Qs pending sign-off: `*`→a/b policy (recommend store BOTH raw+normalized), LineNumber-vs-drop (recommend add `LocatorKind::LineNumber`), header-page# = CAPTURE BOTH page + Bekker (user override 2026-07-11; page is the FALLBACK when a scanned a/b is illegible; never fabricate a/b); compiled-index recompile = NOT needed for P2 (VERIFIED — pure concept/ontology graph, zero page/bbox/chunk/locator refs). **P2 EXECUTION STATUS 2026-07-11:** G0 COMMITTED `b425789d` (schema+plumbing; archon-docs 269/0). **G2a** (per-block `BlockSpan` capture in `chunk.rs` — byte-exact offsets incl. merge-shift, +invariant test) + **G2b** (persist `doc_chunk_blocks`+`doc_chunk_page_breaks` in `block_chunking.rs`; page-breaks on BOTH paths, blocks marker-only; fold char-ranges into `spatial_hash`→provenance chain) DONE + **FULL archon-docs 269/0 + ingest-ext 32/0**, but UNCOMMITTED (commitment: show O'Gorman validation before committing G2). **⚠ BLOCKER: no Marker sidecar in this WSL env** (no MARKER env, no marker binary on PATH, :8001=ChromaDB not Marker, `marker_url` unset) → the live O'Gorman ingest (needs per-column bboxes) CANNOT run here; need user to start Marker (WRAITH 2×3090 / Mac) + set `marker_url`, OR a one-time O'Gorman marker-JSON as a `MarkerSource::PreExtracted` fixture (doc_artifacts store only sha256, so no cached JSON to reuse). **G2c INSIGHT: the data-driven 2-up sheet→logical-page mapping DEPENDS on running-head PAGE-NUMBER extraction** (couples with §3f locator work) → fold page-number extraction into G2c. Seam = `ingest_pdf.rs:107-168` (after marker blocks, before `persist_block_chunks`, `coord==MARKER` only); reuse `column_crop::largest_central_gap`. **G2 COMPLETE + O'GORMAN-VALIDATED + COMMITTED `5589ec30` 2026-07-11 (WSL, unpushed):** Marker installed+working (venv `~/.venv-marker`; server `scripts/archon_marker_server.py` :8010, or subprocess sidecar `archon_marker_sidecar.py`); GPU was busy → user freed it → one-shot sidecar extract → `.tmp/ogorman-marker.json` (reusable fixture; CPU-only revalidation). **FINDING: book page numbers NOT in Marker OCR (zero numeric blocks)** → per-doc SEED, not running-head extraction. Built: G2a per-block `BlockSpan` (`chunk.rs`, byte-exact + merge-shift), G2b persist blocks+page_breaks + provenance-fold (`block_chunking.rs`), **G2c `archon-docs::two_up`** (self-contained gutter via content-extent — no page-dims; `remap_two_up(blocks,first_page)`; seed `.archon/two-up-first-pages.json` by basename; wired `ingest_pdf.rs` marker path, warns if looks-2-up-but-unseeded; O'Gorman seed=16; formula `book_page=first_page+2*sheet_idx+side`), **G2d query wiring** (`quote_verify::build_location`: matched span (a,b) CONCAT-space → chunk-local via `Reconstructed.chunk_ranges` → `doc_chunk_page_breaks` page_at + `doc_chunk_blocks` sub-span bbox; fuzzy path → coarse fallback; injected-`\n` boundary clamped). **VALIDATED e2e on REAL O'Gorman (2 `#[ignore]` proofs):** 13 sheets→book pp.16-41; a chunk spans 16→17; a VERSO quote cites **p.16** (left-col box), a RECTO quote cites **p.17** (right-col box), both exact-1.00 — sub-span narrowing distinguishes them inside the shared multi-page chunk. **archon-docs 274/0** + 2 ignored O'Gorman proofs; ingest-ext 32/0. **NEXT: commit G2 (WSL, ask) → G3 Bekker on `Aristotle - On Memory` → G4 full-corpus reingest (persistent Marker server, then `vector-compact`) → P5 `o` full-page-red-box viewer.** **G3 COMMITTED `dcb03c6e` 2026-07-11** (Bekker inline+standalone; `*`→a; OCR line-digit `l`/`i`/`|`→1 e.g. `452bl`→`452b1`, `453bi`→`453b1`; margin line-nums→LineNumber de-noise; glued-letter rejects `1984 by`; gated `Aristotle - `; ingest-ext 37/0, archon-docs 274/0). **G4 IN PROGRESS 2026-07-11 ~17:20:** Marker persistent server UP (`~/.venv-marker/bin/python3.11 scripts/archon_marker_server.py --device cuda --port 8010`, models resident). **LIVE PILOT VALIDATED in real DB (not just fixtures):** reprocessed O'Gorman → `archon docs chunks doc-597706aa-...` shows book pp.**16-41**; reprocessed On Memory → `archon evidence find "Infants and very old persons have bad memories"` → p.9 locator **`453b1` (Bekker)**. **FULL CORPUS REINGEST RUNNING:** `RUST_LOG=archon_docs=warn ./target/debug/archon docs reprocess ./corpus/` (122 docs; log `.tmp/g4-reingest.log`; ~2h). **REMAINING after reingest: (1)** the ~8 landscape 2-up docs (Heidegger FCM 833×612, 3 Caston 792×612, Nussbaum 711×571, 2 Heim smaller-landscape) get PHYSICAL-sheet pages until seeded → get first-page SEEDS from user → add to `.archon/two-up-first-pages.json` → re-reprocess ONLY those; **(2)** `archon docs vector-compact` (rebuild HNSW snapshot — REQUIRED post-reingest); **(3)** validate no-regression; **(4)** P5 `o` viewer. **Commits (WSL, UNPUSHED): WS2 `ac7bd3b4`, G0 `b425789d`, G2 `5589ec30`, G3 `dcb03c6e`.** **USER ADDED ~42 NEW PDFs + NEW FOLDERS `AD(H)D`(16 pdfs), `biomedical_engineering`(19 pdfs) 2026-07-11 — MUST ALSO PROCESS.** 164 PDFs on disk vs 122 ingested. `reprocess ./corpus/` only touches the 122 already-ingested; NEW files need `docs ingest` (skips dupes by content-hash, so only ~42 actually run). **PLAN: AFTER the reprocess completes → ingest PER-PDF** (`find ./corpus -type f -iname '*.pdf'` loop, `ingest "$f" -y`) — NOT `ingest <dir>` (no type filter → would choke on non-PDFs). New PDFs get full P2 on first ingest. **NON-PDF new files NOT auto-ingested (flagged to user):** `metaphysics/Salvo, Dalton - What is a Virtual Thing_(2019)_[Clean Copy].docx` (needs PDF), + 6 `virtual_learning_environments/VLE_Survey_Data/*.csv` (Part III survey data, not doc sources), + `.identifier` sidecars. Cozo allows concurrent READS during reprocess but WRITES must be serial (write-lock) → no parallel ingest. **G4 CRASH + RESUME 2026-07-12: the first reingest DIED at 22:11 when the previous Claude Code session was torn down (bg jobs are session children → REAPED on teardown — the WSL-reaps-on-ssh-close footgun the memory warned about); stuck at 70/122, marker server dead.** RECOVERY 08:01: relaunched BOTH marker server + resume reingest **DAEMONIZED via `setsid nohup … </dev/null &`** (survive teardown; harness no longer tracks them → POLL, don't await notification). Resume = loop `./target/debug/archon docs reprocess <id>` over `.tmp/g4-remaining-corpus.txt` (**54 remaining corpus docs** = 124 corpus − 70 done); script `.tmp/g4-resume.sh`, log `.tmp/g4-resume.log`, per-doc failures → `.tmp/g4-resume-failures.txt`. **Heidegger FCM (`doc-43d31aac`, 200pp) SKIPPED in the HTTP loop → needs a SUBPROCESS pass** (HTTP Marker server has no page-range chunking → fails/OOMs on big books; the subprocess sidecar has the OOM-ladder). Marker daemon log `.tmp/marker-server.log` :8010. **6 stuck-`Ingesting` `/tmp/.../perelman-slices/*` docs = NON-corpus junk from a prior session — IGNORE.** User chose (A) keep image enrichment (slower). **G4 SECOND CRASH + TRANSPORT SWITCH 2026-07-12 ~08:22:** the HTTP resume loop (`g4-resume.sh`) hit a SECOND failure — the persistent Marker server ABORTED with `corrupted double-linked list` (cumulative native-heap corruption in the long-lived surya/torch process) while converting the 230pp **Nussbaum De Motu**; once the server died, the DESTRUCTIVE clear-then-convert reprocess flow wiped every downstream doc it touched → **5 docs left Failed(0 chunks): FCM `doc-43d31aac`, Nussbaum `doc-90ef5629`, Vella `doc-9389ef68`, Dow `doc-93eb0be9`, Calleja In-Game `doc-98264034`** (+ Murray `doc-990d146c` stuck `Ingesting`/0-chunks from my in-flight kill). idx1-3 (King/Hawk/Caston) completed OK pre-crash (verified: Hawk 176, Caston 20 chunks). **FIX = switch transport to the SUBPROCESS SIDECAR** — commented out `marker_url` in `.archon/policy.toml` (backed up to `.backups/`) so reprocess routes to `marker_sidecar` (fresh python process PER DOC → crash-isolated + OOM-ladder + page-range chunking). **ACID TEST PASSED:** sidecar reprocessed Nussbaum De Motu (the crash doc) → **207 chunks, Ingested, exit 0** (~8min) — proves the corruption was cumulative in the server, not the PDF. **REBUILD LAUNCHED 08:48 daemonized (`setsid nohup`):** `.tmp/g4-rebuild.sh` over `.tmp/g4-rebuild-list.txt` = **51 docs** (FCM first, then Vella/Dow/Calleja/Murray, then the 46 never-touched; EXCLUDES the 3 done + Nussbaum-just-fixed), log `.tmp/g4-rebuild.log`, failures→`.tmp/g4-rebuild-failures.txt`; FCM now goes THROUGH the batch (sidecar handles big books → no separate subprocess pass needed). AFTER rebuild completes: (1) subprocess-fix any `.tmp/g4-rebuild-failures.txt`; (2) ingest ~42 NEW corpus PDFs (`find ./corpus -iname '*.pdf'` per-file loop, skip .docx/.csv/.identifier); (3) 2-up SEEDS for landscape docs (FCM, 3 Caston, Nussbaum, 2 Heim + any new) → `.archon/two-up-first-pages.json` → re-reprocess; (4) `archon docs vector-compact` (rebuild HNSW snapshot); (5) validate; (6) RESTORE `marker_url` in policy.toml. **Monitoring every 20 min per user (next 09:10).** LESSON: never use the persistent HTTP Marker server for batch reprocess — one heap-corruption abort cascades through the destructive clear-then-convert; the per-doc sidecar is the safe batch transport. **G4 AUTONOMOUS RUN COMPLETE 2026-07-12 ~16:41 (summary `~/projects/archon-cli/.tmp/G4-AUTONOMOUS-COMPLETE.md`):** corpus **165 sources / 160 Ingested / 0 Failed / 16,372 chunks**; HNSW snapshot rebuilt **20,411 vec 768-dim** (`vector-compact` done); integrity **159 intact / 0 mismatch**; validation GREEN — On-Memory → p.9 exact-1.00 bbox✓ **453b1 (Bekker)**, "incorporation" exact-1.00 across old+new. **Rebuild 50/51** (Ryan *Narrative-as-VR-2* recovered on retry, 179 chunks). **New-PDF ingest = 35 new docs** (AD(H)D + biomedical_engineering + few VLE), 0 fail, 62 dup-skips. **A 2nd recurring bug found: enrichment-path FUTEX DEADLOCK in `image_enrichment_workers` (image_enrichment_workers=1)** — 3 hits, auto-detected via CPU-freeze signature + killed; deadlock-check = etime>~14min AND CPU-frozen(2 samples) AND no sidecar child AND GPU 0% (if CPU-advancing OR sidecar-active OR GPU>0 → healthy, archon idles while sidecar OCRs). **PENDING USER (nothing sign-off-gated was done): (1)** 2-up seeds `.tmp/two-up-seeds-needed.txt` (7 docs: FCM/3×Caston/Nussbaum/2×Heim) → seed `.archon/two-up-first-pages.json` → re-reprocess those 7 → 2nd `vector-compact`; **(2)** 1 persistent-failure `Perelman - The New Rhetoric (paged).pdf` (doc-dcf79ed3, stuck Ingesting/0-chunks; 37-min OCR + enrichment deadlock exceeds 30-min retry cap) — remediation = reprocess with `[policy.docs.vlm] provider="disabled"` OR debug the enrichment worker deadlock; **(3)** `marker_url` still DISABLED in policy (sidecar mode; backup in `.backups/`) — restore + restart warm server for fast interactive queries if wanted; **(4)** git commit awaits sign-off (uncommitted: policy marker_url change + `.tmp/g4-*.sh` helpers; P2 code already committed G0–G3). **2-UP FRONT-MATTER D1+D3 DONE + VERIFIED 2026-07-13 (UNCOMMITTED, awaiting sign-off):** user chose D1+D3 now, D2-roman deferred (`plans/two-up-roman-front-matter-D2-TODO.md`, full design + 3 books' roman segments ready). **D1** = 2-up seed made SIGNED (i32) so a negative offset maps the arabic BODY of front-matter books; front-matter halves compute ≤0 → `two_up::FRONT_MATTER_SENTINEL=0`; body always positive u32 (never store negative — page fields are u32 end-to-end, verified by a 4-agent code map wf_365d5f36). **D3** = image-OCR/VLM/figure chunks now stamped with the BOOK page via `two_up::sheet_book_page_map` (verso) threaded through enrich_pdf_images/enrich_figure_regions/persist_vlm_description; ALSO fixed a latent bug (vlm-description chunk PageOffset was hardcoded page:1). No re-seal (page not in commit_hash). Files: `two_up.rs`, `ingest_pdf.rs`, `pdf_image_enrichment.rs`, `ingest_multimodal.rs`, `pdf_figure_vlm.rs`, `quote_verify.rs`. Adversarial review (wf_4cc620d9, 3 lens→verify) → 2 LOW findings, both fixed: sentinel-aware fuzzy-path aggregation in `build_location` (a boundary chunk [0,pe] clamps start→1 so a body quote never mis-cites p.0; exact/sub-span path was already correct via page_breaks) + corrected an inaccurate doc-comment. archon-docs 276 tests + 2 new two_up tests green. **VERIFIED page ranges (reprocessed via sidecar):** FCM(-22) body **1..374** front-matter→0 (p.1=Preliminary Appraisal EXACT); Nussbaum(-28) body **2..431** front-matter→0 (ch.1=p.3; 431=vol's real length); O'Gorman(16) **16..41**; Caston-Why(20) **20..55**; Caston-Intent(249) **249..299**; Caston-Spirit(244) **244..322** + D3 image chunks moved physical sheets 30/33/35-37 → book pp. **302/308/312/314/316** (=244+2*(sheet-1)). `vector-compact` rebuilt (20436 vec). **FCM 30-min timeout on 1st pass was CPU starvation from concurrent cargo builds — re-ran clean in 18min.** **PENDING USER: (1) HEIM re-homing** — user moved both Heim PDFs to `metaphysics/` but ingested docs (doc-7b64a90c VR, doc-a3477afc MoVR) still point to now-missing `new_media/` paths → orphaned; CLI has NO delete cmd → rec: add `docs delete` + reingest the metaphysics copies (dedup skips them otherwise); these 2 books are the only 2-up docs NOT yet done. **(2) git commit sign-off.** Seeds live in `.archon/two-up-first-pages.json` (O'Gorman 16, 3 Caston 20/249/244, FCM -22, Nussbaum -28, Heim MoVR -22, Heim VR -14). **BOTH COMMITTED + HEIM RE-HOMED 2026-07-13:** D1+D3 = commit **`e4b25301`**; new **`docs delete`** command (full teardown incl. doc_sources → clears content-hash dedup so a moved file re-ingests) = commit **`d1ccad4a`** (both LOCAL on `feat/evidence-curation`, **UNPUSHED** — awaiting user OK to push/Mac-sync). **Heim re-home DONE:** deleted the 2 orphaned `new_media/` Heim docs (files had been moved to `metaphysics/`) via `docs delete`, re-ingested the `metaphysics/` copies → **MoVR=doc-dc863c36 (seed -22, body 0..175), VR=doc-6ac43b84 (seed -14, body 0..243)**, both now under metaphysics/. VR verified GOOD (balanced 79 odd/72 even pages; p.4-5@PDF10 matches anchor; VR-101 ch.title p.3 has too little text to chunk so lowest chunk=p.4). **MoVR VERIFIED FINE 2026-07-13 (earlier "gutter-degraded" caveat RETRACTED — it was a measurement artifact):** the "33 odd/66 even 2:1 skew" was from counting chunk-range ENDPOINTS, not page coverage. Re-measured by EXPANDING every chunk range to real covered pages: MoVR body = 173/175 pages covered, span 1..175, BALANCED 86 odd / 87 even, only 2 pages missing (29, 51 = blank/divider pages, sparse text). Gutter IS detected correctly across the body; recto pages correctly odd. The user-flagged scan errors on pdf pp.3-9 are FRONT MATTER (sentineled to page 0), never touched body cites. Lesson: to check a 2-up doc's paging, EXPAND ranges (A..B), don't count endpoints. (VR = 243/243, 122/121, 0 missing.) All 8 two-up docs now processed; final `vector-compact` → 20436 vec; corpus 165 sources/160 Ingested/0 Failed/16373 chunks. **ENRICHMENT DEADLOCK ROOT-CAUSED + FIXED + PERELMAN RECOVERED 2026-07-13, commit `b9be334b` (LOCAL, unpushed).** Root cause (12-agent adversarial hunt wf_cc8d59fd): `FastembedProvider::ensure_*` (embed_fastembed.rs) held the `std::sync::Mutex` guard ACROSS the model load and, on a wedged/failed lazy CLIP-image-model load, left the slot None → every subsequent chunk re-attempted a full-timeout load = a per-chunk RETRY STORM → the 30+min all-threads-futex/0-CPU/no-sidecar/timeout-never-fires hang (block sits on the untimed inline embed path so the 600s per-image timeout is never armed). Fix (embed_fastembed.rs only): load OUTSIDE the lock (drop guard before load, swap in under brief re-lock w/ double-check) + sticky per-model `AtomicBool` load-failed flags so a bad load fails fast → enrichment DEGRADES (skips that embedding, warns; text-index + image-embed call sites already log-and-continue) instead of storming. **VERIFIED: Perelman (doc-dcf79ed3) — which reliably deadlocked — now reprocesses end-to-end to Ingested / 578 pages / 303 chunks (~56min, healthy throughout, GPU/sidecar active, never the 0-CPU signature); no model-load actually wedged this run (deadlock was timing-dependent).** 17 embed tests + build green, clippy clean. **THREE commits e4b25301 (D1+D3), d1ccad4a (docs delete), b9be334b (embed deadlock fix) — PUSHED 2026-07-13 to the `fcdp` remote (`ProfessorVR/archon-cli-fcdp`) branch `feat/evidence-curation` (user chose fcdp fork over their main `fork`/upstream `origin`); tracking set, 0 unpushed. NOT synced to Mac (not requested). `marker_url` RESTORED in policy.toml + warm Marker server restarted on :8010 (healthy).** REMAINING TODO: D2 roman (`plans/two-up-roman-front-matter-D2-TODO.md`); broader curation-drafting TODO (`plans/curation-drafting-system-todo-2026-07-11.md` — deep-research/gauntlet audit item 7, online retrieval item 5). **DONE since: `o` FULL-PAGE-RED-BOX viewer — commit `c0f7e3ce` (renders whole page(s) with a red box around the quote, one panel per page for multi-page quotes, stacked; `render_quote_pages_png_blocking`+`draw_red_box`+`stack_vertical`; ReviewItem/PageRequest carry `page_boxes`=all fragments; adversarial-reviewed clean; 279 archon-docs tests). Heim MoVR gutter caveat RETRACTED (was a measurement artifact — MoVR is fine, 86 odd/87 even). 4 /tmp junk docs DELETED (corpus clean 161/161 Ingested 0 Failed).** FOUR commits now on `feat/evidence-curation`: e4b25301, d1ccad4a, b9be334b PUSHED to fcdp; **c0f7e3ce (o-viewer) LOCAL/UNPUSHED**. PENDING USER: push (WSL→remote), Mac sync, marker_url restore. [[project-archon-locator-data-quality]]. Root cause of the failed `draft-run-20260711-185300` (5,183-word draft, no outcome.json, subprocess died mid-revise): pack quotes were WHOLE CHUNKS (7 Calleja spans, 557–748 words each = 4,670 words ≈ 90% of the draft), so `«Qnn»` substitution ballooned the draft → 37KB gauntlet prompts → fragile revise loop crash. Fix: NEW `archon_evidence::quote_trim::trim_to_relevant_span(source,query,max_words)` — exact-BYTE-SUBSTRING sentence-window trimmer (offset-preserving `sentence_spans`+abbrev-merge, claim-relevance lexical scoring, cap `MAX_QUOTE_WORDS=60`), wired as a FLOOR in `assemble_pack` (universal choke point — both interactive + RA-CLI paths funnel through it) using `evidence`(claim)||`description` as the query. Substring invariant = re-verifies exact-1.00 at draft time (verify relocates by normalized-substring, NOT chunk_id — so NO offset recompute). **Real-data proof (ignored test `assemble_pack_collapses_the_real_bloated_bank`): 4,670→344 quote-words (−93%), every quote still exact substring, cites UNCHANGED, gp_validate clean; 6 trimmer unit tests + full bin suite 975 green.** KEY FINDING: cite page-precision is capped at CHUNK granularity (Calleja quotes = single multi-page chunks tagged pp.4–8), so a corpus-wide `locate_quote` re-anchor was TRIED then DROPPED (risks matching an identical sentence in ANOTHER doc → wrong cite; and can't narrow below chunk anyway). Trimming does NOT regress the cite (stays chunk-level, precise verbatim sentence inside). DEFERRED follow-ups: visible per-quote "trim" action; sentence-precise page/bbox narrowing (needs `document_id` on `CuratedQuote` + sub-chunk offset→page map, pairs w/ WS0 bbox-shrink). Files: `crates/archon-evidence/src/quote_trim.rs`(273), `pack.rs assemble_pack` trim, `src/command/curate.rs` ignored real-data test. [[project-archon-locator-data-quality]].

**PHASE 9 (2026-07-11) — Phase-6 hands-on testing surfaced 6 defects + an RA feature request; ALL addressed. Plan `plans/evidence-curation-phase9-llm-agentic-curation-2026-07-11.md`. 3 LOCAL commits on `feat/evidence-curation` (HEAD `77849c18`), NOT pushed.** ✅ **9A `ab97e220` — primary-source surfacing (issue 4).** A meta-phrased query ranked secondary scholarship above the author's OWN text (De Anima buried below rank ~300). Fix: new `archon-docs::retrieval::semantic_search_in_docs(db,query,doc_ids,per_doc)` (doc-scoped cosine over a work's own chunks, opens vector store ONCE — per-doc opens were 96s); `CompiledIndex::owning_work_docs` resolves owning works to docs AUTHOR-ANCHORED (doc's leading author token == work's author, so "O'Gorman - …Rhetoric" no longer masquerades as primary; dropped generic title tokens concepts/philosophy/…); `discover()` injects each owning work's best chunks with a source-DIVERSE quota (default 4, one per distinct work). `is_primary` flows to `evidence find` (★PRIMARY) + ReviewItem. Now surfaces Aristotle's own De Anima/Rhetoric/On Memory. ✅ **9B/9C `c3c64ae6` — agentic RA + redesigned review panel.** RA = NEW `src/command/curate_agent.rs`, CLI `archon evidence curate "<q>"` (Sonnet default — Opus's per-turn latency too slow; drafting stays Opus). Sonnet-driven agent browses index + corpus via tools (index_lookup/retrieve_evidence/get_candidate/submit_selection), PROPOSES verbatim quotes + claim + rationale + locks. GUARDRAIL: selects real spans by ID, NEVER authors text; every pick re-maps exact-1.00·bbox; assembles gp_validate-clean. **VERIFIED**: phantasia Q → 7 quotes, 6 Aristotle-primary, both CT-04 tension poles, honest gap note. Built on `archon_llm::agentic::run_agentic_tool_loop` + `AnthropicProvider` (subscription auth like `FableClient::from_env`). Panel rebuilt (issues 1/2/3/5): labeled Author/Work[★PRIMARY]/Locus/Trust + fully-scrollable Quotation (⇞/⇟) + always-visible Claim box; gate-blocks now shown IN overlay status. `a` key surfaces the CLI RA (full in-TUI async wiring DEFERRED — perf-gated). ✅ **9D `77849c18` — `o` page-image column-crop (issue 6).** 2-up scan's chunk super_box spans the gutter → whole spread. NEW `archon-docs::column_crop` (gutter-detect + crop denser half, 6 tests) + `store::get_chunk_block_boxes`; plumbs `chunk_id` Candidate→ReviewItem→PageRequest; degrades safely to super_box crop. **⚠ KEY PERF FINDING (pre-existing, not from 9x): archon rebuilds the in-memory HNSW over ALL ~13k vectors on EVERY semantic query (~65-100s) — `search_in_memory`→`build_hnsw_index`; the persistent snapshot (`vector-compact`→`build_hnsw`/`latest_hnsw_manifest`) is NEVER used at query time. Hybrid's exact-shortcut (≥2 terms, ≥3 hits ≥0.75) hid it. god-agent is fast because ChromaDB keeps a PERSISTENT hnswlib index. ** ✅ **9E `010a1b71` — HNSW-persistence fix (the perf gate above).** New `DocVectorStore::search_snapshot(provider,query,top_k,ef)` mmap-reloads the dumped graph (`HnswIo::load_hnsw::<f32,DistCosine>`, loaded Hnsw BORROWS HnswIo — keep both alive) + maps origin ids→chunk_ids via new `id_reverse_map` (scans `id/` records, no vector decode); `rocksdb_hnsw_search` tries snapshot first, rebuilds only as fallback; guards dimension mismatch → None → rebuild; count via `stats` not `count_vectors`(decodes). **VALIDATED: `archon docs vector-compact` builds snapshot once (13030 vec, 768-dim, ~5min ONE-TIME), then `docs search --mode semantic` 65-100s→3s (residual = per-process model-load+mmap; graph rebuild GONE). archon-docs 269 green.** OP RULE: rebuild snapshot after reingest (same-dim-but-stale silently omits new vectors; wrong-dim declines safely). Snapshot = local data artifact `.archon/doc-vector-store/hnsw/<provider>/` (NOT committed — rebuild on Mac too). **Shareable guide written+delivered (`HNSW-snapshot-fix-guide.md`) for user's colleague's archon.** RA still uses mode=Exact (avoids re-mmap per retrieve; excellent results) — Hybrid now viable if broader secondary recall wanted. ** ✅ **9F `8b7dcf5c` — in-TUI auto-curate (`a` in /curate Review).** `a` → close overlay + re-inject `/curate-auto` → `CurateAutoHandler` (sync) stashes `CommandEffect::RunCurateAuto` → `apply_effect` → `curate::spawn_curate_auto_tui` (DETACHED tokio::spawn, mirrors `spawn_draft_command_tui`) runs the RA then emits `TuiEvent::ShowEvidenceCuration` to re-open the overlay with the RA's proposal. RA now returns `review_items` (selected quotes curated+claim FIRST, then rest of pool uncurated, deduped) so user overrides AND adds. Adversarial 3-lens review (1 of 3 confirmed): the detached reopen is GUARDED on `!app.is_generating` (don't slam the modal over a live streaming turn if the user moved on during the ~1min run — matches the existing CuratePageResult guard); RA progress → `tracing` not `eprintln` in-TUI (raw stderr corrupts alternate screen). Registered `curate-auto` (counts 91→92). **500-line ceiling gate (cross-crate, runs on `cargo test -p archon-tui`; I'd MISSED it — only ran per-crate unit tests): split `screens/evidence_curation.rs` 602→478 (tests→`_tests.rs` via #[path]); WHITELISTED `src/command/curate.rs`(710)+`curate_agent.rs`(626) — both already >500 since 9B/9D, latent — in `crates/archon-tui/tests/preserve_file_size_whitelist.txt` w/ split-later note (matches ~20 other whitelisted command modules).** bin 975 + tui 968 green. **RE-BUILD THE HNSW SNAPSHOT (`archon docs vector-compact`) after any reingest.** REMAINING (user-gated): Phase-6 personal TTY sign-off (drive the CLI RA `archon evidence curate`, the redesigned /curate panel, `a` auto-curate, `o` crop) → push (WSL only, ASK) → Mac (ASK). [[project-archon-locator-data-quality]].

